From 720b5827a090cb24182cb49932ebaf34c783b9ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:58:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 371/371] DOS-PORT: patch 0371 -- lever L1: route-cache
 pre-warm in the room-load / restore stall (DOSAGS_ROUTE_PREWARM, default off)

Why: in Maniac Mansion Deluxe the first walk click after a save restore and after entering room 2 pays the legacy
pathfinder's cold per-mask analysis (0211's normalised mask + 0319's labels): 63 and 187 ms of route search at
DOSBox-X fixed 40000, 233 and 370 ms of logic on the 486 (dosags docs/lab/LAB-RB.md section 3.2). The room is still
faded out a few ticks earlier, when that work costs no visible frame.

What: DOSAGS_ROUTE_PREWARM unset or 0 = off (the 0370 head; the default); exactly "1" = on; any other value = off.
When the FadeIn event is processed (ac/event.cpp; after a new room's BeforeFadein event and after a save restore,
inside the stall tick, before the fade-in) the engine prepares the walkable mask for the player character
(prepare_walkable_areas, as move_character_impl does) and calls the legacy finder's unchanged is_route_possible() once
on it, source = destination = the first walkable pixel (LegacyRouteFinder::DosPrewarm). That runs exactly the 0211
analysis and the 0319 labels the first request on that mask would run, and records the same mask serial. The request
path is untouched: every request still matches the cache by serial or byte compare, or rebuilds it, so a mask changed
after the warm (a character moved, a script, a DrawingSurface) is caught as before. MaskRouteFinder gains one virtual,
DosPrewarm, with a no-op default (the JPS finder of >= 3.5.0 games keeps no such cache). is_route_possible gains
observation-only counters, no logic change. All of it is under __DJGPP__.
Witness: "DOS-PORT routeprewarm DOSAGS_ROUTE_PREWARM=<v|(default)> mode=<0|1>" from init_room_pathfinder; "DOS-PORT
routeprewarm_final mode= prewarms= built= matched= nowalk= skipped= us= max_us= first_serial= first_compare=
first_miss= first_none= pending=" in RUNMANI.LOG in both flavours. DOSAGS_ROUTE_PREWARM joins the RUNMANIFEST env
allowlist. Lab lever: dosags docs/lab/LAB-L1R.md (lab-l1r.diff), landed unchanged but for the comments and the
__DJGPP__ guards around its counters in route_finder_impl_legacy.cpp.

Gates (DOSBox-X fixed 40000, every tick rendered, frame digest + PRESENT_VERIFY, seeded, R2 at its 0370 default in
both arms; dosags tests/harness/results/L1LAND-2026-11-08): off vs on EQUAL on every loop counter of MMD fixtures G
(3164), V (3964), GCL (7004), H (7004), the intro (1299) and AGS Quest AutoPilot (3558), each cell also EQUAL to
LAB-L1R's; the warm served the first request by serial in H (2), G and GCL (1 each), was built and never asked in V and
the intro, and is a no-op for AGS Quest's JPS finder. Controls: a stale warm stamped as current DIFF (6285/7004); a mask
change right after the warm EQUAL on vs off (the first request rebuilt), DIFF with the cache re-stamped (5124). "on"
and "2" read as off. Release, on vs off: 5 Days room 3, Trilby room 35, AGS Quest game output EQUAL; P9-shape MMD with
it unset EQUAL to the 0370 release. +3073 bytes instrumented, +2561 release; both flavours byte-identical across two
clean builds.

